4,"_81":82,"_83":135,"_85":136},{"_74":127,"_76":128,"_78":128,"_79":129,"_81":82,"_83":130,"_85":131},{"_74":122,"_76":123,"_78":123,"_79":124,"_81":82,"_83":125,"_85":126},{"_74":117,"_76":118,"_78":118,"_79":119,"_81":82,"_83":120,"_85":121},{"_74":112,"_76":113,"_78":113,"_79":114,"_81":82,"_83":115,"_85":116},{"_74":107,"_76":108,"_78":108,"_79":109,"_81":82,"_83":110,"_85":111},{"_74":102,"_76":103,"_78":103,"_79":104,"_81":82,"_83":105,"_85":106},{"_74":97,"_76":98,"_78":98,"_79":99,"_81":82,"_83":100,"_85":101},{"_74":92,"_76":93,"_78":93,"_79":94,"_81":82,"_83":95,"_85":96},{"_74":87,"_76":88,"_78":88,"_79":89,"_81":82,"_83":90,"_85":91},{"_74":75,"_76":77,"_78":77,"_79":80,"_81":82,"_83":84,"_85":86},"slug","skills/level-design/templates/review","title","Level Review Template","label","description","Review a level's goals, spatial flow, readability, encounters, technical limits and next revisions using a reusable checklist.","group","More notes","source","docs/skills/level-design/templates/review.md","sourceHash","779a2edb6080480f4b73ad9b96692b9ae7eb4aa3e2f1bd613c637b4240ee608b","skills/level-design/templates/playtest-report","Playtest Report Template","Record a playtest's task, observed behavior, participant comments, blockers and follow-up checks without mixing evidence and interpretation.","docs/skills/level-design/templates/playtest-report.md","1fefc9190edd9a460a263033c12f79b555e4fb7ef3e139bfb75d7ca5061ff8a2","skills/level-design/templates/level-brief","Level Brief Template","Fill in a level brief with player intent, scope, routes, encounter goals, constraints and observable acceptance criteria.","docs/skills/level-design/templates/level-brief.md","21ca07d5e829cc7bb4bd2719ae24d9d8bfe2e71e1c607526e0907aacabad9927","skills/level-design/references/wayfinding-playtesting","Wayfinding, Player Understanding, and Playtesting","Test how players understand a space using observed routes, wayfinding cues and playtest evidence rather than designer assumptions.","docs/skills/level-design/references/wayfinding-playtesting.md","778c6d2ab5095aa2a794c5b84da4cdef575350af9b235ca983c5e1a2a0307c6e","skills/level-design/references/tools-quake","Tools, Resources, TrenchBroom, Quake, and File Formats","Review TrenchBroom, Quake workflows and level file formats with the tool and engine boundaries each requires.","docs/skills/level-design/references/tools-quake.md","62d3e4393042b8338c0655724e19b9f2e3f654c6e314e05516dd2e9c2cc46392","skills/level-design/references/spatial-layout","Layout, Flow, Verticality, Critical Paths, and Gates","Shape critical paths, alternate routes, gates, verticality and flow around the choices a player should make.","docs/skills/level-design/references/spatial-layout.md","e8641eb15099627cf59978304ef807c5ade18f886bd02e8519739c2405249e6a","skills/level-design/references/source-map","Source Map and Reading Coverage","Trace the level-design skill's topics and adaptations to the original Level Design Book reading coverage.","docs/skills/level-design/references/source-map.md","0e0bf748565ed9da345e0f2a01261a6cc5ea8af80933a21389b3f79ef9742ca0","skills/level-design/references/scripting-doors","Scripting, Navigation, and Doors","Specify scripted interactions, navigation dependencies and door states with readable feedback and recoverable behavior.","docs/skills/level-design/references/scripting-doors.md","31194f2df5c662e41fa292b6ee820bbc594a22ec421cdea1f6cba207b5a2a2eb","skills/level-design/references/optimization-release","Optimization, Documentation, Packaging, and Release","Prepare a level for release through performance work, documentation, packaging and checks on the target build.","docs/skills/level-design/references/optimization-release.md","c861e21126e62c18971e1f0ced575cf4f6605fdf9e3310d753ccd85b377fc9ca","skills/level-design/references/lighting-art","Lighting, Darkness, Environment Art, Texturing, and Storytelling","Use lighting, darkness, materials and environmental storytelling to support navigation, readability and the intended experience.","docs/skills/level-design/references/lighting-art.md","ce11613f8c7efe1ab46a656e34fbfe837dea9e2cda21eb8b65c5dd7ab29e1d90","skills/level-design/references/learning","Learning, Teaching, Exercises, Critique, and Portfolios","Use exercises, critique, teaching methods and portfolio evidence to develop and explain level-design decisions.","docs/skills/level-design/references/learning.md","dfcd003181de23901a8944c7af364311108a4c66f1a7daf1d2c2409ccd0382b0","skills/level-design/references/foundations","Foundations, Pre-production, Research, Worldbuilding, and Scope","Set player intent, research questions, worldbuilding constraints and project scope before drawing a level layout.","docs/skills/level-design/references/foundations.md","79cc3bd4a123904fad9309d7444fd27d62287fe1307e1529a60104f493ce8b5a","skills/level-design/references/culture-history","Level Design as Culture and Historical Practice","Place level-design practices in their cultural and historical context instead of treating familiar conventions as universal rules.","docs/skills/level-design/references/culture-history.md","fec0df471ced497b20c5e0ccd08340f3ac3297393ac618cff7626256333f4d0a","skills/level-design/references/combat-balance","Combat, Enemy Roles, Encounters, Cover, and Map Balance","Design encounters around enemy roles, sightlines, cover, movement and multiplayer balance, then test the resulting decisions.","docs/skills/level-design/references/combat-balance.md","bdbe6945e7cd9a51aa50ad9a1b02fac12635f9ec8f0f187c1753abba871033c8","skills/level-design/references/case-studies","Studying Levels and Transferring Their Relationships","Study existing levels by reconstructing spatial and gameplay relationships, then adapt those relationships to a new brief.","docs/skills/level-design/references/case-studies.md","4f0643c5d776144531ec46b2af1936158eea6780aa84751d74b0ca61237a52b0","skills/level-design/references/blockout-metrics","Blockout, Massing, Landscape, Composition, and Metrics","Plan graybox massing, terrain, composition and player-scale metrics before committing to finished environment art.","docs/skills/level-design/references/blockout-metrics.md","aba747e2d92c367001c3f3c6b5b4027472926beac9dff33882025c6a631c1898","zh/publishing-platforms","发现游戏，发布自己的作品","发行与游戏平台","从官方入口了解 Steam、itch.io 等游戏平台，分清试玩、下载、源码与发行状态。","中文指南","docs/zh/publishing-platforms.md","bbfd4f281d7377ff703903e7a1503a5a420965545e029bb85d35b81af95bd977","zh/deployment","在本地运行和发布 GameMap","本地运行与部署","在本地启动 GameMap，了解源资料自动刷新、生产构建预览与 GitHub Pages 部署方式。","docs/zh/deployment.md","3af68ff1e53b13f73eed4af5e8128f12bc4afe4da809267a0c8446abb2485079","zh/level-design-skill","关卡设计 Skill","了解关卡设计 Skill 的适用范围、下载入口、简报与试玩模板，以及来源和非商业许可条件。","docs/zh/level-design-skill.md","fcf46c19f6167fb34c8fa4a2026f10b72566ce61dcf6e02abf616f719b2ccb7c","zh/practical-guide","从想法到可玩的游戏","用一个无需安装依赖的 HTML 小游戏跑通开始、游玩、胜负与重试，再完成一次边界明确的修改。","docs/zh/practical-guide.md","f1d7c3b06c422562e82bb2998ea580d1a084529325f1d7e719cc0f98b015c1ae","zh/reading-guide","怎样使用这份资料库","怎样使用资料库","按当前问题选择工具、案例或研究资料，分清来源、可运行性、许可与实际验证范围。","docs/zh/reading-guide.md","2177ae41d02ce8ed282e0dea85820cbf86a6cc0a8d19be9656fe105d98564a6b","skills/level-design/LICENSE","Attribution, License, and Adaptation Notice","Skill attribution & license","Read attribution and CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 reuse conditions for the unofficial Level Design Book skill adaptation.","Skills & practice","docs/skills/level-design/LICENSE.md","7baf28f0942b105ddcf68f80f73dfbdba24d7207f60e6876ddb99d28d417e3a6","skills/level-design/SKILL","Level Design: From Intended Experience to Tested Space","Level design skill","Route a level-design task from player intent and research through layout, grayboxing, playtesting and revision.","docs/skills/level-design/SKILL.md","81c8dd3c0237982e39772cd3d778e4d258d0c1a7ace0fe74daf7cd6994702f27","content-model","Content model and coverage contract","Content model & coverage","Understand registered content kinds, source ownership, localization, generated outputs and completeness checks.","About this atlas","docs/content-model.md","c9840507e5663eb52fd682b4464418a0575d0af7e5a8ab1649fbf4b6b5c71d97","icon-sources","GameMap resource logo sources","Logo sources","Find the official sources, local files and attribution records for resource logos and visual identity assets.","docs/icon-sources.md","2a0dc49ab2d3cdc562167054937b8a2936fbbe664377393e09e00846c45363d2","media-sources","GameMap demo media sources","Media sources","Trace project previews and recordings to their original creators, capture methods, credits and reuse limitations.","docs/media-sources.md","8eb13ad83a837c9d34ad7aa863989bcf17e0c57cd1a2b2afe8aaca8a468db42a","contributing","Contributing to GameMap","Contributing","Contribute resources and game cases with primary evidence, accurate source scope, runnable access and clear attribution.","CONTRIBUTING.md","7daedb965be711a10e1e472942af4e17f5639ce77011c67f51c0abda45fddc5a","catalog","Awesome AI Game Development","Full resource catalog","Browse the complete resource catalog with categories, source links and scope notes for AI-assisted game development.","AWESOME.md","b0d58b0f5a8da338f4e7e186f4df92b6ecc376a4793bed5d98802e98ba9c77a8","overview","GameMap","Project overview","Explore GameMap, an OpenEnvision project connecting AI game-development tools, playable projects and practical production knowledge.","README.md","4f238c9d10e302cfb7ee0f5cc5df468bfac22018399653df5fa12f9d153e63d4","community-case-research","Community AI game case review","Community case research","Inspect the research log behind community game cases, including source completeness, AI attribution, play checks and rejected candidates.","Evidence & evaluation","docs/community-case-research.md","49b064a6562b255de7c9aecbc8bf3112a36370f568306e46783ae454e3412838","source-revision-notes","Source revision and implementation boundaries","Source revisions","Trace research claims to reviewed source revisions and distinguish stable release evidence from moving documentation.","docs/source-revision-notes.md","d074761cd7ff667d22331b02a2e9ca843831c4525a411757700e5c9d8cedf896","catalog-review-coverage","Catalog review coverage","Review coverage","Read the catalog's source-review ledger, including verification scope, rejected claims and remaining coverage gaps.","docs/catalog-review-coverage.md","b0021a07ffa9c64b4d90fd53d2353d52e7904f52eb71408e76c995b673a4f001","agent-interface-evidence","Coding-agent game interfaces: source evidence","Agent interfaces","Review engine-agent interfaces for permissions, observations, reset behavior and evidence of the operations they actually expose.","docs/agent-interface-evidence.md","7510f6ff8fdce7d3ba4b1ea35befc17cfc7796b9f826d4157b166817a300b582","gameplay-state-contracts","Gameplay state, narrative checkpoints and durable effects","Gameplay state","Specify durable gameplay state across saves, retries, narrative transitions, cancellation and restored world effects.","docs/gameplay-state-contracts.md","39daa242fce97cd61aa619a90f35ec12f314b9adf8a59936546967fa46bca50e","benchmark-reproducibility","Reproducing game-development benchmarks","Benchmark reproducibility","Audit game-agent benchmarks by environments, actions, resets, seeds, versions and the evidence needed to reproduce a result.","docs/benchmark-reproducibility.md","4ff4a210639b7e3f49a024faa488424bbf45bae2d95517fdf3b9ad0d4bdf0133","game-development-evaluation","Additional evaluation research for agents that create games","Development evaluation","Choose evaluation tasks and metrics that distinguish code completion, game behavior, visual quality and player experience.","docs/game-development-evaluation.md","e294011f80cbdce3f3931c408edbc1d7de355ba27dfb811e6741d3bae317d9df","visual-feedback-mechanisms","Visual-feedback mechanisms for game-creation harnesses","Visual feedback","Design a visual feedback loop that joins observations, task context, proposed edits and checks without treating an image as proof of success.","Assets & generative tools","docs/visual-feedback-mechanisms.md","9800f24df8b5f7e859c46ed058400152ed23f501ba83e3e4a2362eede6d6aac8","visual-evidence-research","Visual evidence and agent-harness research","Visual evidence","Choose screenshot, segmentation, video and frame-readback evidence with explicit capture identity and observation limits.","docs/visual-evidence-research.md","160171b2f4332bba01be76fa6b5d3bcd64e56367e0a55ca9835fd9ada6f26aa8","asset-selection-feedback","Asset candidate selection and visual-feedback creation","Asset selection","Turn asset search and review into a bounded selection process with candidate identity, reasons, feedback and acceptance checks.","docs/asset-selection-feedback.md","04f504b0bf14a4df47005642258b4e7510addb575c690ab855f678710fa0d06e","asset-validation-contracts","Asset interchange and validation contracts","Asset validation","Validate sprites, tilemaps, meshes, rigs, collision, materials and audio against the runtime behavior each asset must support.","docs/asset-validation-contracts.md","5a2c80a8b3ca37f1fb0a26de94023a602355b13e32e2b4d613ba9f69d934abd8","generation-delivery-contracts","Generation jobs, artifact delivery and asset acquisition","Generation & delivery","Track generated jobs and artifacts through retrieval, cancellation, provenance and delivery to an engine or content pipeline.","docs/generation-delivery-contracts.md","81be65c35e61babf8933d2cba4163c292a1a6b6eeeb94e9bb36af38e799fb619","generative-api-boundaries","Generative API and model boundaries","API boundaries","Check authentication, job lifecycle, quotas, output access and usage conditions before integrating a generative service.","docs/generative-api-boundaries.md","64f71410f530db6da3bca0aaa3f9c99a706540272af989db252075102e582817","generative-tools-research","Generative tools: additional source-reviewed research","Generative tools","Review generation tools by the assets they produce, their documented interfaces and the work still required for game integration.","docs/generative-tools-research.md","4780eb1f63fa2300d03d3f4c3c4858f6a07639b0e66e7a78f1e30d47bbcdd611","production-coverage-gaps","Production coverage and remaining work","Coverage & limitations","See which production interfaces and evidence contracts are documented and which executable integrations remain unfinished.","Production & engineering","docs/production-coverage-gaps.md","3cb5daf6bf9e4dd28c0f26a79f08e6c9f1f3d4f3bc897401dd03ee207f99cf3f","production-debugging-contracts","Production debugging and evidence contracts","Debugging contracts","Match profiler, GPU, physics, memory and build evidence to a specific failure and a repeatable diagnostic task.","docs/production-debugging-contracts.md","a54714123e7a1ca1937f0ca687565d4a069d52d4014bab162f862517c8ea28f3","native-operation-details","Native operation details and lifecycle boundaries","Native operations","Look up native commands and lifecycle boundaries for import, rendering, input, audio, dialogue and browser captions.","docs/native-operation-details.md","f6b2d944a9c4cfa8ea937d120aee0e1d50b6b85a9981964185268febecb68d13","studio-production-case-studies","Studio production case studies and acceptance lessons","Studio case studies","Translate documented game-studio engineering accounts into proposed workflows while preserving each source's scope and limits.","docs/studio-production-case-studies.md","56eeef744a25f7a377eb797ebb4f669685f2b3b356e3e29342085902346459b7","production-work-orders","Production work orders: artifacts, recovery and acceptance","Production work orders","Adapt bounded production task templates for asset integration, navigation, multiplayer, builds and other engine workflows.","docs/production-work-orders.md","c612e8d796834f907606b68a7d90d3f75eabdf5ef5f14b0f2842dbe2a53985e2","engine-operation-contracts","Engine operations: completion, recovery, and evidence","Engine operations","Define engine operations with explicit inputs, completion, failure, cancellation and persisted output instead of relying on tool success messages.","docs/engine-operation-contracts.md","36f9e2afea2659af26299d81f3165bb22a8dcc940622cfb78b27bee6458fc0a2","production-research-notes","Production tools and acceptance boundaries","Production research","Connect production-stage tools and interfaces to concrete artifacts, completion signals and the gaps that still need testing.","docs/production-research-notes.md","b713a8ed1f662d7f79708cd4363cd3580c0a980757e15638aa1467c0506b25b2","research-index","Production research dossiers","Research overview","Navigate production research by task, from engine operations and asset delivery to state, debugging and evaluation evidence.","docs/research-index.md","e1d872b4e5982d699ceda5e95eb031b2650b40447eec59540d938f1a6e2a9872","world-model-notes","Coding World Models: Categories, Selection, and Research Notes","World models","Distinguish executable code worlds, hybrid renderers, neural simulation and generated 3D scenes, with release and hardware limits.","Explore the ecosystem","docs/world-model-notes.md","3284ce6c39421d88858bdb0919306f1aa14a2c4334245530a70943f0bed9a741","cadle-repositories","Cadle-like repository research import","Cadle-like repositories","Inspect a source-reviewed ledger of Cadle-related games, browser projects, engines and agent harnesses, including unresolved candidates.","docs/cadle-repositories.md","8b51b2695a82da4a37bc0a69e39d8fdb5b6637476e15e9dd99f4500b2ad6a0e3","game-ai-notes","2D / 3D Game Development AI: Research Notes","2D & 3D development","Review AI contributions across 2D and 3D development, including executable interfaces, version limits and evaluation claims.","docs/game-ai-notes.md","ffcb9a080adca25301db04bba859b2faf2336ee85cc8d383d2bd81126f9d9b2d","engines-notes","Engines, rendering libraries, and content tools: sources and scope","Game engines","Compare game engines, rendering libraries and content tools by runtime role, source status and integration needs.","docs/engines-notes.md","f9ccc0288b0c600d0bdd576528966abf34d5dd1226cb4c6e0019a19